{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Mechanism confirmed, fix applied, RED -> GREEN and teeth both proven.\n\nDETERMINISTIC-VS-INTERMITTENT: intermittent, load-sensitive. Under 36x CPU oversubscription\non an 18-core host, the unfixed test failed 8 of 30 consecutive runs (~27%), which closely\nmatches the ~2/9 per-ubuntu-cell rate observed in CI. Post-fix, the identical load harness\ngave 0 of 30.\n\nThe 8 pre-fix failures showed the deadline race in three shapes, all one cause:\n  - `assert 'worker_timeout' == 'worker_failure'`  ([overflow-worker_failure], the CI param)\n  - `assert 'worker_timeout' == 'binary_replaced'` ([replace-binary_replaced])\n  - `assert 'abstain' == 'match'` at line 344      (the trailing retry, [nonzero], [replace])\nThe `JSONDecodeError` seen in CI is the narrower sub-case where the SIGTERM lands inside the\nchild's non-atomic `capture.write_text`.\n\nEMPTY-CAPTURE WINDOW, measured directly by sweeping `_run`'s deadline across the child's\ncapture-write moment (40 runs per deadline):\n  deadline=0.03  missing=10  EMPTY=2   complete=28\n  deadline=0.04  missing=0   EMPTY=3   complete=37\n  deadline=0.05  missing=0   EMPTY=2   complete=38\n  deadline=0.06+ missing=0   EMPTY=0   complete=40\nAn EMPTY (not missing) capture.json is exactly the `json.loads('')` precondition.\n\nCHILD COST: median 39 ms, p95 42 ms, max 307 ms over 30 idle samples — a 0.2 s budget is only\n~5x the median with a tail that already crosses it on a fast host.\n\nCI-SIDE CORROBORATION: in failing job 101290521991 the coverage report lists\n`src/rebar/grounding/terraform_corroborator.py` line 301 — the `raise _Abstain(\"worker_failure\")`\n— as UNCOVERED for the whole job, so the overflow case never reached the stdout-size check.\n\nSEEDED-DEFECT PROOF (teeth): with the fix in place, deleting the\n`len(stdout) > MAX_STDOUT or len(stderr) > MAX_STDERR` guard at\nsrc/rebar/grounding/terraform_corroborator.py:300-301 makes [overflow-worker_failure] FAIL with\n`AssertionError: assert 'config_inspect_schema_skew' == 'worker_failure'`; restoring the guard\nreturns all 4 params to green. The parametrization now genuinely exercises the branch it names.\n\nPUSH-VS-PR: confirmed exactly. Run 33960153355 (pull_request) checked out `refs/pull/137/merge`\n— `HEAD is now at 3ad6f66 Merge 00b0faa67956... into 59d504c2bdbb` — while sibling push run\n33960151040 resolved the branch head `00b0faa67956` alone and passed. The branch predates\n59d504c2bdbb, so the PR run was the first execution of this test against a tree containing it.\nThe dependabot bump is not implicated.\n\nNOT the missing-binary story: this test points PATH at its own fake-binary directory\n(`monkeypatch.setenv(\"PATH\", str(bin_dir))`), so the audited terraform-config-inspect is\nirrelevant to it, and its exception comes from the harness reading its own capture.json\n(test file line 186), not from the corroborator parsing tool stdout. Separate defect from\nwidish-chemic-goitered.\n\nFix: scope the shortened DEADLINE_SECONDS to `mode == \"hang\"` (raised to 1.0 s), and make the\nfixture child's capture write atomic (staging path + os.replace). No product change; no\nassertion weakened."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788608441776351335,"uuid":"542474c6-4705-4868-abff-23b799adf8e4"}